\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Dollar And DEM In Slow Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1997\par 11:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening just a bit against the dollar and the Deutsche mark in calm trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 1053 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 170.46 to 170.51 forints, up from up from 170.33 to 170.38 forints in late trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 103.15 to 103.18 forints, up from 103.09 to 103.12 forints. \par \par \uc2  'The market's quite slow,' said Attila Behan, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ING Bank Hungary Rt. in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Because the forint's fortunes on the market are closely tied to movements in the dollar against the mark, Behan said U.S. durable goods orders data scheduled for release at 1330 GMT could move the Budapest market. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 170.48 forints, up from 169.11 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 103.10 forints Tuesday, compared to 103.39 forints Monday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Wednesday's fixing will be released after 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates have dropped below 22% Wednesday. The three-month rate is indicated at 21.97% Wednesday, compared to 22.02% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1056GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1t00kf4\p