\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakens Vs Dlr; Market Seen Eyeing U.S. Data \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 1997\par 14:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in late trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 1310 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 170.33 to 170.38 forints, up from 169.16 to 169.21 forints in mid-session trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 103.09 to 103.14 forints, down from 103.26 to 103.29 forints. \par \par \uc2  'The market hasn't been that active,' said Szilvia Kucsera, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Hungarian Foreign Trade Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Kucsera said that in trading against the dollar Tuesday the forint has stayed within 20 basis points from its strongest position on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  Volume could pick up later in the day as market participants watch for employment cost index data from the U.S., due out at 1330 GMT, Kucsera noted. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 170.48 forints, up from 169.11 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 103.10 forints Tuesday, compared to 103.39 forints Monday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 22.02% Tuesday, compared to 22.05% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1312GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1s00mb1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picsc