\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Down Vs Dollar; Further Weakening Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1996\par 12:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is sharply weaker against the dollar and is also weaker against the Deutsche mark Wednesday, in a market described as thin and jumpy by one trader. \par \par \uc2  At 1119 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 160.24 to 160.29 forints, up from 159.48 to 159.53 forints in midsession trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 102.70 to 102.75 forints, up from 102.29 to 102.35 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at a relatively weak point of around 1.87% below the midrate on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  'It's a very thin market, and because of that there are just a few players, and they've really been pushing (the forint) around,' said Peter Way, chief dealer at Unicbank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Way noted that December is 'a funny month' because of market participants' need to cover their year-end positions. He said it wouldn't be surprising to see the forint slide a bit further against the dollar, but said profit-taking would eventually stop the forint's decline. \par \par \uc2  'There are a couple of banks leading the market, and the rest will just have to swim with the flow,' Way said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 163.37 forints, up from 161.78 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 104.42 forints Tuesday, compared with 104.98 forints Monday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% ECU (European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit). Wednesday's fixing will be released at 1200 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 22.41% Wednesday, compared with 22.75% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-12-96 \par \par \uc2  1139GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsc401kmm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
