\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary's Forint Weakening Vs Dollar, Stronger Vs DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 1996\par 12:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark on a lack of fresh news Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 1046 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 155.72 to 155.77 forints, up from 155.18 to 155.23 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 102.05 to 102.08 forints, down from 102.12 to 102.16 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading against the dollar near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  On the open market, volume Friday has been moderate, said Istvan Gere, forint dealer at ING Bank in Budapest. As usual, trades involving the forint have been driven by developments involving major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  'The only news moving the market today is the dollar-mark trading,' Gere said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 158.93 forints, down from 159.54 forints Tuesday. It fixed the mark at 104.63 forints Thursday, compared to 104.45 forints Tuesday. Markets in Hungary were closed Wednesday in observance of a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% ECU. Friday's fixing will be released at 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 23.13% Friday, compared to 23.11% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-10-96 \par \par \uc2  1050GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \u