\par\par \b \uc2  Forint eases against dollar in slow trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 16 (Reuter) - The Hungarian forint eased against the dollar in slack early trading, reflecting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight firming against the mark, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The forint opened at 151.00/05 to one dollar, down from Thursday's closing 150.90/95. The forint lingered at this level in the first forty minutes of trading. \par \par \uc2  "The forint got slightly weaker, because the dollar/mark figure went up slightly," ING Bank's Attila Behan said. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats in the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made up of 30 percent dollar and 70 percent Ecu. \par \par \uc2  The forint opened at the NBH resistance level and was not seen drifting away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Thursday's news that Trade and Industry Minsiter Imre Dunai is quitting the government did not affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "This did not have any impact here, foreign investors are not frightened by the quitting of a minister of industry, they regard the long-term government policies as important," Behan said. \par \par \uc2  -- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8g044ov\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
