\par\par \b \uc2  Forint ends steady, BCE yen and Swiss franc active. \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 12 (Reuter) - The Hungarian forint closed unchanged against the dollar on Monday, mostly tracking dollar/mark movements on international markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The forint finished at its opening level of 149.95/150.00. \par \par \uc2  "Things were really quiet, with the forint remaining close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level (bid) for most of the day," said Jozsef Bodor of West LB Hungaria. \par \par \uc2  "Some dollar buying this morning moved the unit around 10 pips from the bid, but it fell back by the close," he said, adding that the bigger influence remains the dollar/mark cross on international markets. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, made up 30 percent of the dollar and 70 percent of the Ecu, and moves within a 4.5 percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band set by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In mostly dull \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures trading at the Budapest Commodity Exchange (BCE), the yen was the most active with 60 percent of the 161.4 million turnover. Swiss francs were also active. \par \par \uc2  -- Duncan Shiels, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8c04fra\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
