\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary's Forint Weakening Vs Dollar, Higher Vs DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1996\par 12:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in early trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0927 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 150.18 to 150.23 forints, up from 149.37 to 149.44 early Monday. They quoted the mark at 100.96 to 101.01 forints, down from 101.25 to 101.30 forints. \par \par \uc2  On the open market, traders said the forint is trading at the bottom of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5% \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its overnight active repo interest rate to 29.00% from 29.25% Monday, but traders said the reaction was muted. \par \par \uc2  'There's been no reaction on the spot market yet,' said Akos Dolle, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Citibank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The bank also cut the one-week passive repo rate to 23.00% from 23.35%, the one-week active repo rate to 29.00%, from 29.25%, and the one-month passive repo rate to 23.50% from 23.75%. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the Hungarian National Bank fixed the dollar at 152.89 forints, down from 153.03 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 103.60 forints Monday, compared to 103.45 forints Friday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% ECU. \par \par \uc2  Forint interest rates were 23.50% to 24.00% Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-08-96 \par \par \uc2  1010GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8606ek2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picsca