\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  Won't Widen  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Band: Banker o-dji e-bdj123 \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 1996\par 16:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not widen its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, according to the vice president of the Hungarian National Bank (MNB), the Hungarian News Agency (MTI) reported Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The vice president, Laszlo Csirjak, said he was acting to quell rumors that the bank might widen the band. \par \par \uc2  'I think it's good news,' said Geza Pollanyi, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at OTP Bank in Budapest. 'The market has been stabilizing since March and this decision promotes stability.' \par \par \uc2  Csirjak said that a wider band could lead to an 'undesired revaluation' of the Hungarian forint. Csirjak also said that a wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was incompatible with \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 'crawling peg' devaluation policy. That policy in effect amounts to a fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, Czirjak said. \par \par \uc2  An instrument of monetary policy, pegging is stabilizing the price of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a market. At present, \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 'crawling peg' policy, which was adopted in March, limits the maximum monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to 1.2% a month. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1552GMT \par \par 