\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary's forint weakens slightly against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Feb 2 (Reuter) - The Hungarian forint closed the Friday session of the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at 141.97/142.02 to the dollar, slightly weaker than its 141.85/95 opening. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian unit, which closed Thursday at 141.90, moved slightly away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resistance level. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Hungary fixed its midday dollar midrate at 145.05 forints, giving a bid of 141.78 forints. \par \par \uc2  "We expected the forint to weaken further as long-term interest rates have been falling, but two major commercial orders from major banks slowed the slide," said Ervin Csengeri of Inter-Europa Bank. \par \par \uc2  Csengeri added that he expects the forint to move further inside the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent wide floating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range next week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures turnover on the Budapest Commodity Exchange slumped to 92.4 million forints from Thursday's 2.01 billion. Most contracts were for September marks and Ecus. \par \par \uc2  -- Duncan Shiels, Budapest newsroom (361) 266 2410 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds22035sm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
