\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary's forint firms against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, December 13 (Reuter) - Hungary's forint closed at 136.61/66 against the dollar, slightly firmer from its opening at 136.75/80. \par \par \uc2  "The forint was mostly influenced by the dollar/mark and the Ecu's crosses with the dollar and the mark abroad and nothing on the domestic market, otherwise it was pinned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid," said Citibank's Peter Benda. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, made up of 30 percent mark and 70 percent Ecu, in the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said its relatively high interest rates made the forint attractive compared with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The NBH fixed its noon dollar midrate at 139.74, which determined its bid at 136.60. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's firming against the Ecu in the morning was reflected in rising dollar and dropping Ecu prices on the Budapest Commodity Exchange's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, where turnover fell to 676 million forints from yesterday's 2.23 billion. \par \par \uc2  -- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drcd00tvu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
