\par\par \b \uc2  HUNGARY FORINT ENDS LOWER. \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Sept 8 (Reuter) - The Hungarian forint finished lower in quiet business with players content to react to dollar-mark fluctuations in arbitrage trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We followed the dollar-mark movements, there were no other factors," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The forint ended at 131.45/55 forints to one dollar compared with 130.80 yesterday and 131.09/14 at the open today. \par \par \uc2  The bid of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range stood at 131.40/50 forints. Dealers said they had seen no sign of NBH \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Last month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a rare open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the forint drifting too far away from the bid. \par \par \uc2  The NBH fixed the midpoint of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range at 134.50 forints. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures on the Budapest Commodity Exchange surged with volume totalling 3.486 billion forints, the second highest in the exchange's history. Most of the 30,100 lots of volume was in the longer maturities. \par \par \uc2  Mark contract settlement prices eased, while dollars rose. Yen and interest rate futures also saw some turnover. \par \par \uc2  -- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040129dr9800mok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
