\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian forint ends slightly higher. \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Sept 5 (Reuter) - The forint closed slightly firmer versus the dollar as the mark strengthened against the U.S. unit in afternoon trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We were tracking the dollar-mark, close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid," a dealer said. At the close, the forint was quoted at 130.00/05, compared with its 130.13/17 opening. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the midpoint of its 4.5 percent floating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 133.13, against 132.66 yesterday. The NBH's bid was calculated at 130.13. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates are dropping on the interbank market, which may result in money pouring into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and boosting the forint in the next few days," said Istvan Hideg of Takarekbank. \par \par \uc2  Dollar and yen futures on the Budapest Commodity Exchange remained stable or dropped, while some mark futures rose, tracking movements on international markets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market was active as last week's announcement of a monthly 1.2 percent forint devaluation in 1996 boosted trade in 1996 maturities. \par \par \uc2  -- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr95047bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
