\par\par \b \uc2  Forint firms vs mark following Buba rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 24 (Reuter) - The forint firmed versus the mark following news the Bundesbank had cut leading interest rates by 50 basis points, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We closed before lunch at 87.70 forints to one mark and and now we have risen to 87.55," Inter-Europa Bank's Ervin Csengeri said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 130.80 forints in early afternoon compared with 130.10 before lunch. \par \par \uc2  "But turnover is low, I would say the reaction was muted," Csengeri said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the forint was still pinned to the bid of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent-wide floating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  The midpoint of the range was set at midday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 133.06 forints to one dollar. The midpoint is calculated against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basked consisting 30 percent of dollars and 70 percent of ECU. \par \par \uc2  The bid stood at 130.77 forints to one dollar in early afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The forint opened today at 130.10/20 and closed yesterday at 129.80. \par \par \uc2  -- Budapest editorial (36 1) 266 2410 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr8o04pmk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
