\par\par \b \uc2  HUNGARY FORINT UNCHANGED, SEEN STABLE. \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 9 (Reuter) - The forint was left unmoved by the fluctuations of interbank interest rates yesterday and today, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At open, the forint was quoted at 125.38/43 to the dollar, against yesterdays open at 125.50/55 and close at 125.30/35. \par \par \uc2  The midpoint of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent wide floating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band stood at 128.24, the bid was calculated at 125.35. \par \par \uc2  "I feel the forint is stable, and even the changes in the interbank interest rates in the last two days could not influence it," said Peter Luczo of Inter-Europa Bank. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Hungarian overnight rates dropped to 29.25 percent, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the reverse repo rate to 29 percent from 30. Rates soared to 31.5 percent today as banks concentrated on tomorrows tax payment deadline. \par \par \uc2  The forint has been pinned to the bid for months, with the exception of a few short periods, when the demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared, but then fell equally quickly. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Today will not be an exception, the forint will be stuck to the resistance," said Agnes Nagy of Altalanos Ertekforgalmi Bank.\tab     -- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom +361 266 2410\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (c) Reuters Limited 1995\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040129dr8900j55\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
