\par\par \b \uc2  FORINT SWINGS AGST DOLLAR AS DOLLAR/MARK CHANGES. \b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, May 12 (Reuter) - The forint swang wildely today against the dollar, closely tracking the mark's roller-coaster ride on international markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit closed at 122.85/90 forints against its open at 122.85/00 forints against its close yesterday near 121.00. \par \par \uc2  The midpoint of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range was set at 125.56 forints to the dollar, up from 123.24 yesterday. This midrate determined a 122.73 bid. \par \par \uc2  "The forint moved 100 points each way or so, just as the mark moved," said Peter Benda of Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "But compared to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket (made up of 30 percent dollars and 70 percent ECUs), we were almost entirely stable," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian unit has been bouncing against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid for weeks because of forint illiquidity in the banking system. \par \par \uc2  Turnover was near average, Benda added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab     -- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266-2410\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (c) Reuters Limited 1995\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040129dr5c00m3z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
